Remove Adjacent Duplicate Characters

Description

This Java program removes adjacent duplicate characters using a Stack.

How It Works

- "push()" adds a character to the Stack.
- "peek()" checks the top character.
- "pop()" removes a character when two adjacent characters match.
- "StringBuilder" builds the final String.

Example

Input: "abbaca"

Output: "ca"

Time Complexity

O(n), where n is the length of the String.

Data Structure

Stack<Character>
